        ],
        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "Thermal behavior of the polymers was studied using dynamic mechanical thermal analysis (DMTA). By increasing the temperature from 30 to $3 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$, one transition was seen for the polymers at which tan d went through a maximum. This transition was related to the glass transition temperature of the polymers. Also DSC analysis confirmed data obtained from DMTA. The glass transition temperature $( T _ { \\mathrm { g } } )$was taken as the midpoint of the change in the slope of the baseline. Also, no polymer showed a clear melting endotherm which resulted from the amorphous nature of the polymers. Thermal analysis of the polymers is summarized in Table 3 and the representative curves of DMTA for 1AQA-PPDI $( T _ { \\mathrm { g } } =$1908C) and DSC for 1AQA-MDI $( T _ { \\mathrm { g } } { = } 1 7 8 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } )$are shown in Figs 4 and 5, respectively. The glass transition temperature of 1AQA-PPDI was higher than 1AQA-MDI due to the more rigidity of PPDI with respect to MDI structure."
      },
